    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Execution / Initial Foothold", "technique": "T1204 + T1036", "what_happened": "At 2027-03-29 01:18:42 CEST, Sysmon Event 1 on FIN-WS-07.corp.local (10.30.6.84): a new process 'cdn_helper.exe' was created with parentImage=C:\\Windows\\explorer.exe under user=CORP\\karim.b. The binary lives at C:\\ProgramData\\Update\\cdn_helper.exe — an unusual path for a 'CDN helper'; legitimate CDN-related clients normally ship inside vendor folders under C:\\Program Files\\<Vendor>\\. The binary is UNSIGNED (signed=false) and the SHA256 hash is c8d1a2b3e4f506172839405a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c. parent=explorer.exe means the implant was launched from the user shell (double-click, shortcut, or recent-startup item) rather than a service. The path 'C:\\ProgramData\\Update' masquerades as a Windows-Update-adjacent location to blend in.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1: image=C:\\ProgramData\\Update\\cdn_helper.exe + parentImage=C:\\Windows\\explorer.exe + signed=false + user=CORP\\karim.b. Path masquerading + unsigned + writable user-controlled directory = high-confidence implant indicator (MITRE T1036 Masquerading + T1204 User Execution).", "first_seen": "2027-03-29T01:18:42+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Command and Control (Initial Beacon)", "technique": "T1071.001", "what_happened": "At 01:22:10 CEST (3m 28s after process start), Suricata logged an HTTP_GET from src_ip=10.30.6.84 → dest_ip=104.21.55.62 with host=cdn-updates-check.com, uri=/api/v1/ping, user-agent='Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64)'. The destination IP is Cloudflare CDN-range (legit infrastructure abused for C2). The user-agent is the default Edge/Chromium browser banner — implants commonly clone this UA to blend with normal web traffic. The path /api/v1/ping is a typical heartbeat / check-in endpoint, NOT a static-asset CDN fetch path.", "chain_reason": "Suricata HTTP log: data.src_ip=10.30.6.84 + data.dest_ip=104.21.55.62 + host=cdn-updates-check.com + uri=/api/v1/ping. The temporal proximity to step 1 (3m 28s) and the suspicious URI structure flag this as the first C2 check-in.", "first_seen": "2027-03-29T01:22:10+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Command and Control (Periodic Beacon Pattern)", "technique": "T1071.001 + T1029", "what_happened": "Between 01:22:10 and 01:42:10, Suricata logged 5 identical HTTP_GET requests from 10.30.6.84 → 104.21.55.62 to host=cdn-updates-check.com /api/v1/ping at TIMESTAMPS 01:22:10, 01:27:10, 01:32:10, 01:37:10, 01:42:10 — interval EXACTLY 300 seconds (5 minutes) with ZERO jitter across 5 consecutive requests. The Wazuh network-anomaly decoder emitted a NETWORK_BEACON ALERT: 'protocol=HTTPS, interval=300s, host=FIN-WS-07, 5 consecutive beacons detected'. Pure fixed-interval periodicity with no jitter is the signature of a low-and-slow implant heartbeat; legitimate browser / app traffic exhibits substantial inter-request variance.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh decoder NETWORK_BEACON ALERT, plus 5 Suricata HTTP events with identical src_ip / dest_ip / host / uri / user-agent at 300-second deltas. Pattern-of-life signature: interval-stability < 1% across 5+ requests to a non-categorized domain = scheduled C2 beacon (MITRE T1029 Scheduled Transfer + T1071.001 Web Protocols).", "first_seen": "2027-03-29T01:22:10+0200"},
